config BCM2835_SDHC
	bool "BCM2835 / BCM2710 / BCM2837 Arasan SDHCI host controller"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_BRCM_BCM2835_SDHCI_ENABLED
	select SDHC_SUPPORTS_NATIVE_MODE
	# Data path is driven by the external BCM2835 DMA engine via DREQ
	# (the Arasan core's CAPABILITIES register reads zero on this silicon
	# so SDMA / ADMA2 are not available). DMA pulls in CACHE_MANAGEMENT
	# for buffer flush/invalidate around transfers (see
	# feedback_zephyr_sys_cache_needs_cache_management).
	select DMA
	select CACHE_MANAGEMENT
	help
	  Enable the Broadcom BCM2835-family Arasan SDHCI host controller
	  driver. Drives the EMMC port that's wired to the BCM43430A1
	  wireless chip on Pi 3 / Pi Zero 2 W. Polled control path (no IRQ
	  yet); data phase moves bytes through the external BCM2835 DMA
	  engine via DREQ 11. R1b/R5b deferred.

if BCM2835_SDHC

config SDHC_BCM2835_SELFTEST
	bool "Run an SDIO bring-up self-test in driver init"
	default n
	help
	  After the driver has reset the controller and configured the
	  bus to 400 kHz / 1-bit / 3.3 V, fire CMD0, CMD5 (inquiry +
	  op_cond), CMD3, CMD7 and a CMD52 CCCR read through the driver's
	  own request() path. Logs each step; does not fail init on
	  command errors (the device stays available for later layers).
	  Used during BCM43430A1 bring-up to verify the request path
	  end-to-end before wiring up the Zephyr SDIO subsystem. Disable
	  in production builds.

endif # BCM2835_SDHC
